Welcome to OOFEM Extractor manual README.

What is here
------------
The manual of the extractor tool (``tools/extractor.py``), which reads selected
values from an oofem output file and either prints them step by step or checks
them against reference values.  It also documents how the record syntax of the
``errorcheck`` export module, used by the regression tests, differs from that
of the tool.

Prerequisities
----------------
To build the documentation, you need Sphinx (Python documentation generator,
https://www.sphinx-doc.org).
Typically invoke ``pip install -U Sphinx`` to install it on your system.

Building the PDF additionally needs a LaTeX installation; see doc/README for
the list of packages.

Building documentation
----------------------
1) Change working directory to doc/extractorInput inside your oofem source tree
2) run ``make html`` to build the html version, in ``_build/html``
3) for the pdf version run ``make latex``, then ``make all-pdf`` in
   ``_build/latex``

If a change does not seem to take effect, run ``make clean`` first: the build
reuses the parsed documents cached in ``_build/doctrees``.

Conventions
-----------
Record and parameter names are written as plain ``literals``, so that they
carry the tinted background the stylesheet gives them, and actual input is
shown in a ``.. code-block:: none``.  The parameters of a record are listed in a
``list-table`` with an explicit ``:widths:`` option.  The other manuals follow
the same conventions, so keep to them when adding text here.

The manual describes what ``tools/extractor.py`` and
``src/core/errorcheckingexportmodule.C`` actually accept; when either of them
changes, update the corresponding page.

Links to the other manuals are plain absolute URLs to the published HTML on
www.oofem.org; there is no intersphinx inventory shared between the manuals.

Shared configuration
--------------------
Project metadata and the shared html settings come from ``doc/global_conf.py``,
and the page width and figure sizing from ``doc/_static/oofem.css``.
``html_static_path`` must keep ``../_static``, so that the shared stylesheet is
still copied.  See section [4] of doc/README.

Happy contributing!
